course: dictionary
lesson: 5356
title: Kindly, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «She smiled kindly» means she smiled in a warm, gentle way. «Kindly close the door» is different: here kindly is a polite way of saying please.
explain: Look at the job the word does. In «a kindly old man», kindly describes a person, so it means kind and friendly. In a notice like «Kindly keep off the grass», kindly means please, and it can sound a little strict.
explain: Some words belong to phrases. «Not take kindly to» means not like something, so «He did not take kindly to being told to wait» means he did not like it. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Kindly can be an adverb: in «She smiled kindly», it tells how she smiled.
fact: Kindly can be an adjective: in «a kindly old man», it describes a kind, friendly person.
fact: «Kindly» means please in formal notices and letters, as in «Kindly close the door».
fact: «Not take kindly to» means not like something.
exercise: «Telling a grown-up kindly about a little brother's copied homework helps him learn.» What does kindly mean here? | *In a gentle, caring way | Please, in a formal way | In a rude, loud way | Very quickly
exercise: «Kindly keep off the grass.» What does kindly mean in this notice? | Not liking it | *Please | In a gentle way | Like a kind old man
exercise: In «a kindly old man», what kind of word is kindly? | A verb | *An adjective | A noun | An adverb
test: «The Rat kindly looks the other way.» What does kindly show about the Rat? | He is running away | He is hungry | He is angry with the Mole | *He is gentle and caring towards the Mole
test: In «a kindly old man», kindly means? | Quickly | *Kind and friendly | Unhappy | Please
exam: In «He did not take kindly to being told off», what does not take kindly to mean? | *Did not like it | Heard it quickly | Was very kind about it | Said please
